  "the field is bufferLength in X_ITE 16.6.0 and bufferlength (lowercase l, output only) in the X3D 4.0 XSD and UOM; both names exist here and the test uses the X_ITE one at run time, because the XSD one cannot be written",
  "loading from url is written (fetch and decodeAudioData, then numberOfChannels, sampleRate, bufferLength, buffer and bufferDuration are filled in) but not tested here: it needs a sound file",
  "a pause stops the source and resume starts it again at the paused position, since a Web Audio buffer source cannot pause",
  "autoRefresh and autoRefreshTimeLimit are held, not acted on",
  "X_ITE 16.6.0 reports bufferDuration -1 (not the UOM's 0) from the start while load is TRUE and nothing has loaded; the bridge does the same"
